Trans:
For Ukrainian refugees in Poland, the rules for residence and assistance have changed:
- Ukrainians can stay free in temporary shelters only for the first 120 days from their first arrival;
- Starting from May 2023, they will need to cover 75% of living expenses;
- Social payments during departure from the country will be frozen. If the stay outside Poland exceeds 30 days, the social status will be lost.

